  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "krb5 security update",
      "Title": "Synopsis",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for krb5 is now available for openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "Kerberos is a network authentication protocol. It is designed to provide strong authentication for client/server applications by using secret-key cryptography.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nMIT Kerberos 5 (krb5) through 1.22.2 contains a NULL pointer dereference in make_cred_list() in rd_cred.c that allows authenticated Kerberos clients to crash services by sending mismatched KRB-CRED arrays. Attackers can send forwarded credentials with more tickets than ticket_info entries through gss_accept_sec_context() to crash GSS-API acceptor services, causing denial of service.(CVE-2026-107778)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for krb5 is now available for openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of medium. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "Medium",
      "Title": "Severity",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "krb5",
      "Title": "Affected Component",
      "Type": "General"
    }
  ],
